  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 60af0432a3c869e48a591344a8dafd71, type: 3}
  m_Name: PatApp_1
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  question: "After months of appointments, tests, and treatments, your trial has
    come to an end. After your last study visit, you\u2019re talking with a close
    friend who came to support you. They say, \u201CWell, since the trial has ended,
    your role as a patient participant has also ended, right?\u201D\nIs this true
    or false?"
  explanation: Patient participants often continue to play a role even after the
    trial ends. Researchers may check in with these patients about long-term effects,
    and many patients choose to share their experiences to improve future trials
    and/or to help other patients considering participation. The patient voice remains
    essential beyond the end of a single study.
  correctAnswer: False
  incorrectAnswer1: True
  incorrectAnswer2: 
  incorrectAnswer3: 
  questionRole: Patient
  questionType: TrueFalse
  questionStage: Approval
